  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing Humanitarian Assistance among the Most Drought-Affected Communities and Support Their Resilience Building</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this project, IOM is providing humanitarian assistance and building resilience among the most vulnerable communities severely affected by the drought and resource-based conflict in Kenya. The project is focusing on four intervention areas: 1. Increasing knowledge of the Government of Kenya and humanitarian partners on drought-induced displacement, including resource-based and inter-communal conflict dimensions, for targeted and comprehensive humanitarian assistance; 2. Reducing vulnerability of the drought affected population to food insecurity and improving access to safe water; 3. Improving community resilience to resource-based conflict in target counties; and 4. Building capacities of policy makers at county level to review policies and structures to reduce vulnerability of displaced population due to climate change and conflict induced by climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
